<description>
Extend each solid foreground rectangle toward its same-color isolated pixels with capped one-cell paths, clearing each original marker pixel.

Input structure
- The background is the dominant color.
- Each foreground color has exactly one solid rectangular object and one or more isolated same-color marker pixels.
- Every marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the rectangle bbox and lies outside it.
Rule
- For each marker, draw a one-cell-wide straight path from the adjacent side of the rectangle through one cell beyond the marker.
- Add a three-pixel perpendicular cap at the rectangle end and around the marker endpoint.
- Recolor the original marker pixel to background.
Key insight
- The isolated pixels are not copied; they mark the hollow endpoints of capped protrusions grown from their matching rectangle.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "solid foreground rectangles and same-color isolated marker pixels",
  "path": "straight horizontal or vertical path from the aligned rectangle side to one cell beyond each marker",
  "trajectory": "paint a one-cell-wide path with three-pixel perpendicular caps at the rectangle side and marker endpoint",
  "transform": "clear each original marker pixel to background; keep the rectangles unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13-30 rows x 16-30 cols
  background: single dominant color
  foreground_colors: 1-3 distinct colors, each != background
  per_color:
    rectangle: exactly 1 solid filled rectangle, min dimension >= 2, max dimension 2-11
    markers: 1-3 isolated single-pixel markers of same color
    marker_alignment: each marker is axis-aligned with rectangle bbox (shares row-span XOR col-span), outside the bbox
    marker_offset: marker's aligned coord is >= 1 from both edges of the rect span (room for 3-cell cap)
    marker_distance: 3-10 cells from nearest rect edge to marker
    same_side_spacing: same-side markers need aligned-coord diff >= 3 (non-overlapping caps)
  clearance: entire protrusion area (path + caps + 1-cell-beyond) must be background in input; no overlap across colors
  output_rule: |
    Per marker, draw 1-wide path from rect side to 1 cell beyond marker.
    Add 3-cell perpendicular cap at rect side and 2-cell cap flanking marker.
    Clear original marker pixel to background.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size, background, 1-3 foreground colors.
    2. For each color, choose rectangle dims (h x w, both >= 2) and place it with generous margin.
    3. For each color, choose 1-3 marker targets. For each marker pick a side (top/bottom/left/right) and an aligned coord >= 1 from rect edges. Pick distance 3-10.
    4. Compute full protrusion (path + caps) for each marker. Verify all protrusion cells are background and in-bounds; reject on overlap.
    5. To form input: place rectangles and marker pixels only (no protrusions). To form output: apply protrusions and clear markers.
```
</generation_spec>
